      "content": "11.5 Examiner Favorites :One-Liners"
    },
    {
      "id": "pxlxknc",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Punjab is called the 'Granary of India' or 'Breadbasket of India'.",
        "The state animal of Punjab is the Blackbuck; state bird is the Baz (Goshawk).",
        "Ludhiana is called the 'Manchester of India' for its textile industries.",
        "Mandi Gobindgarh is the 'Steel City of Punjab'.",
        "Jalandhar is called the 'Sports City of India'.",
        "Kapurthala is called the 'Paris of Punjab' for its French-style buildings.",
        "Patiala is famous for Patiala Peg (large whisky measure), Patiala Salwar, and Jutti.",
        "The first Battle of Panipat (1526) established Mughal rule in India :fought near Punjab.",
        "Punjab produces ~40% of India's wheat procurement annually.",
        "SGPC (Shiromani Gurdwara Prabandhak Committee) headquartered at Teja Singh Samundari Hall, Amritsar.",
        "The Radcliffe Line divided Punjab in 1947; Sir Cyril Radcliffe drew the boundary.",
        "Punjab Police Training Academy is located at Phillaur (Jalandhar district).",
        "Punjab has 23 districts organized into 5 divisions.",
        "The SYL (Sutlej-Yamuna Link) canal dispute is between Punjab and Haryana over river water sharing.",
        "Bhagra Nangal Dam is on Sutlej river; Gobind Sagar reservoir is its reservoir in Himachal Pradesh.",
        "Harike Wetland (Hari-ke-Pattan) is India's largest wetland in NW India; Ramsar site.",
        "Chandigarh, the capital, was designed by Swiss-French architect Le Corbusier in the 1950s.",
        "Punjab's Scheduled Caste population (~32%) is the highest proportion of any Indian state.",
        "The Jallianwala Bagh Memorial was established in 1951; memorial well and eternal flame present.",
        "Operation Blue Star (June 1984) was ordered by PM Indira Gandhi; Lt. Gen. K.S. Brar commanded.",
        "Punjab Police Act 2007 established Accountability Commissions for police oversight.",
        "Bhagat Singh was born on September 28, 1907 at Banga, Lyallpur district (now Pakistan).",
        "Udham Singh (born Sunam, Sangrur) shot Michael O'Dwyer in London on March 13, 1940.",
        "The Ghadar Party was founded in 1913 at San Francisco by Sohan Singh Bhakna and Lala Hardayal.",
        "Guru Granth Sahib was first compiled in 1604 (Adi Granth); final version completed at Damdama Sahib, Bathinda.",
        "Anandpur Sahib Resolution (1973) :Akali Dal demand for greater autonomy for Punjab; religious place for Sikhs."
      ]
    }
